+
+## GLM kept prompts in host RAM (TF_GLM_KEPT_HOST, TF_GLM_HOST_CACHE_GIB)
+
+`families/glm5_next/cuda/kept_host.py` and its call sites in `multi.py` (`_keep`, `_admitted`, `_resume`, `_evict`,
+`_drop`, `admit`, `health`) and `engine.py` (the `--parallel` pool formula) follow the design of glm53f-afd's host RAM
+tier, by Hugh Madden ([@dangerm00se](https://github.com/hughmadden)),
+[glm53f-afd](https://github.com/hughmadden/glm53f-afd) @ `91db3cc`, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Turquoise Bay AI
+Pty Ltd: `crates/glm53f-coordinator/src/hostcache.rs` (page-locked slabs carved into fixed-size slots; a snapshot's
+KV rows and its positional state, the KDA recurrent states and convolution windows, in host RAM; RAM eviction least
+recently used first), `crates/glm53f-coordinator/src/scheduler.rs` (a snapshot the GPU evicts for room is stored to
+RAM first; a prompt that misses the GPU restores from RAM instead of prefilling) and `docs/RUNNING.md` ("KV snapshots
+and the RAM tier"); glm53f-afd credits mimo26f-afd's DS41RT host snapshot cache for it. Only the design is taken; no
+code is copied (glm53f-afd is Rust and CUDA; this is written on TensorFold's pool and extents). Changes: a kept
+prompt's state goes to host RAM when it is kept (glm53f-afd moves it under pressure), which gives the 5090's pool the
+bytes from startup; rows park in pages of the pool's 2,048-token alignment, per kept prompt (no page sharing between
+prefixes); the tier is only on the AFD attention node (world 1). With both switches unset, pool, kept prompts and calls
+are the ones before.
